---
title: Inner Loop Lifecycle
config:
    layout: elk
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> ready_for_dev: from process refinement
    [*] --> ready_for_experiment: from process refinement
    [*] --> ready_for_spike: from process refinement
    [*] --> ready_for_hotfix: from process mitigation

    state "Feature / Bug / Chore" as dev_group {
        ready_for_dev --> implementing: developer claims issue
        implementing --> ready_bounced: developer bounces ticket
        implementing --> pr_review: developer requests PR review
        pr_review --> staged: from process pr-review (PR merged)
    }

    state "Experiment" as exp_group {
        ready_for_experiment --> implementing_experiment: developer claims experiment
        implementing_experiment --> pr_review_experiment: developer requests PR review
        pr_review_experiment --> staged_experiment: from process pr-review (PR merged)
    }

    state "Spike" as spike_group {
        ready_for_spike --> implementing_spike: developer claims spike
        implementing_spike --> spike_completed: developer posts spike findings
    }

    state "Hotfix" as hotfix_group {
        ready_for_hotfix --> implementing_hotfix: developer claims hotfix
        implementing_hotfix --> pr_review_hotfix: developer requests PR review
        pr_review_hotfix --> staged_hotfix: from process pr-review (PR merged)
    }

    ready_bounced --> [*]: to process refinement

    staged --> [*]: to process release (standard train)
    staged_experiment --> [*]: to process release (standard train)
    staged_hotfix --> [*]: to process release (hotfix patch train)
    spike_completed --> [*]: to process refinement

    note right of ready_for_dev
        Cross-process legend:
        • Entry shared states: ready_for_dev, ready_for_experiment (from refinement); ready_for_hotfix (from mitigation). Same work item continues from the other diagram.
        • Entry spawn events: ready_for_spike (from refinement — consultant spawns a new spike sub-issue). Starts fresh on this diagram.
        • Exit shared state: ready_bounced (to refinement). Same issue re-enters refinement.
        • Exit spawn events: spike_completed notifies the parent issue's consultant on refinement; no new work item.
        • Exit external handoffs: staged / staged_experiment / staged_hotfix → release lifecycle. These are external because the release lifecycle tracks a different unit of work (the release train), and the issue is merely a member of the train.
    end note

    note right of implementing
        Developer opens a draft PR at claim time, not at code-complete. CI runs against draft while coding.
        See pr-lifecycle for the PR's own states (draft, needs_review, reviewing, needs_qa, merging).
    end note

    note right of pr_review
        Resting on this diagram. The ticket stays here for the entire PR review + QA + merge cycle — changes requested, QA fails, re-review, merge conflicts all happen within the PR lifecycle without advancing the ticket's state. The ticket only advances to staged when the PR is merged.

        This keeps principle 6 clean: PR review mechanics live on pr-lifecycle.mermaid, not here.
    end note

    note right of ready_bounced
        Shared resting state with refinement. Developer claimed ready_for_dev/experiment/hotfix, evaluated, and decided the issue is not ready. They do NOT bounce from the resting queue — they claim first, then bounce (principle 3).
    end note

    note right of staged
        "Staged" = PR merged to main. NOT yet in production. The issue is added to the currently-accumulating release train. See release-lifecycle for what happens next.
    end note

    note right of staged_hotfix
        Merging a hotfix PR triggers the release lifecycle to open a hotfix patch train (single-issue train). IC bypasses the release gate.
    end note

    note right of spike_completed
        Spike's deliverable is the findings comment. No release, no deploy, no user impact. Returns to refinement so the parent issue's consultant can claim.
    end note

    note right of ready_for_spike
        Spawn event (not shared): the consultant on refinement creates a new spike sub-issue. The spike starts its lifecycle here on inner-loop — refinement does not render ready_for_spike. The parent issue rests on refinement in `spiking` during this time.
    end note

    note right of ready_for_hotfix
        Shared resting state with mitigation. IC created the hotfix issue during an incident. Hotfix skips refinement — scope is defined by the IC on creation. Claim SLA: minutes.
    end note
